course: dictionary
lesson: 14090
title: Melancholy: a quiet, lasting sadness
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Melancholy means a deep, quiet sadness that lasts for a while. It is not loud or sudden. «Her melancholy lasted for days after her best friend moved away.» The sadness stayed with her for a long time, and it was quiet rather than angry.
explain: Melancholy can also be an adjective, a describing word. It tells you that something makes you feel sad. «The old song sounded melancholy.» The song is the thing that brings the sadness, so melancholy describes the song.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Quiet, slow, empty and grey words point to melancholy. «A melancholy wind blew over the empty beach.» The empty beach and the wind tell you the mood is lonely and thoughtful, not cheerful.
fact: Melancholy is a literary word, so you will often meet it in poems, stories and music.
fact: «Melancholy» can be a noun meaning a deep, quiet sadness that lasts a while.
fact: «Melancholy» can also be an adjective, meaning sad or making you feel sad.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, the Mock Turtle is very melancholy, sighing and sobbing as he tells his story.
fact: Melancholy is quiet and thoughtful, while miserable is a sharper, more painful kind of unhappy.
exercise: «The old song sounded melancholy.» What does melancholy mean here? | Very fast | *Sad, making you feel a gentle, thoughtful sadness | Angry and rude | Loud and bouncy
exercise: «On rainy afternoons he sits by the window, lost in melancholy.» What is melancholy in this sentence? | A loud shout | *A deep, quiet sadness that lasts a while | Happiness | A quick game
exercise: Which clue in «The Mock Turtle sighed and sobbed as he told his melancholy story» shows he is sad? | *Sighed and sobbed | The word story | The word as | The word told
test: «A melancholy wind blew over the empty beach.» Which word is a clue that the mood is quiet and lonely? | Blew | Beach | Wind | *Empty
test: Ella says melancholy means very angry. Is she right? | Yes, it means furious | *No, it means a deep, quiet sadness | Yes, it means cheerful | No, it means noisy
exam: What does melancholy mean? | Very fast running | Very happy | A kind of hat | *A deep, quiet sadness that lasts a while
